  "headline": "Nasdaq-100 futures hold within Thursday's settle range into the deep European pre-open as Asia runs firmer than the prior run (Kospi +2.7%, Nikkei +1.4%, broad AI/semiconductor strength led by SK Hynix +6% and Kioxia +7%) -- VIX ticks to a fresh recent low near 14.5, 10Y ~4.65% -- with today's Retail Sales (12:30 UTC) and cash open still the session's main checkpoints; Alpha Vantage remains fully rate-limited for a third consecutive run, so this assessment again relies entirely on WebSearch.",
  "body": "About one hour past the prior run and roughly 7.5 hours after Thursday's 20:00 UTC cash close, conditions remain calm into the deep European pre-open. NQ futures trade around 30,177, inside Thursday's post-close range of roughly 30,124-30,232 and modestly below today's session open near 30,201; S&P futures sit around 7,825, inside a 7,774-7,839 range -- both consistent with a quiet overnight handover and no confirmed gap or failed-pullback structure. Asia's session runs firmer than the prior run: Japan's Nikkei 225 is up about 1.4% (versus +0.8% last run), South Korea's Kospi is up roughly 2.7% and approaching 7,000, and the move is broad-based in AI/semiconductor names -- SK Hynix +6%, Kioxia +7%, Samsung Electronics +2%, SoftBank +5% -- an overnight rally in US stocks and continued soft-inflation, Fed-hold bets are cited as the driver. This further confirms that Applied Materials' own tepid post-earnings stock reaction (AMAT beat on revenue, profit and guidance but fell on shrinking China revenue and a demanding valuation after a roughly 108% year-to-date run) remains company-specific rather than a broader semiconductor-equipment or AI-capex read-through; no evidence of sector-wide transmission has surfaced across two runs. The VIX has ticked down to a fresh recent low near 14.5 (from ~14.6-14.7 last run) and the 10-year Treasury yield remains around 4.65%, essentially unchanged; oil is likewise little changed from Thursday's close (WTI ~$81.25, Brent ~$87.07). Geopolitically, the Strait of Hormuz standoff continues unresolved -- Iran's parliament still reviewing a bill to bar US/Israel-linked vessels pending war-damage compensation, and vessel traffic through the strait remains far below pre-war levels -- but no new kinetic escalation has been identified since the prior run; the Ukraine-Russia war likewise continues without a fresh market-moving escalation, with Russian forces making incremental territorial gains and both sides continuing to trade strikes. Alpha Vantage's free-tier daily quota remains exhausted for a third consecutive run -- the TREASURY_YIELD call was retried once and returned an immediate rate_limit error both times -- so, per the fallback protocol, this assessment again relies entirely on WebSearch for yields, oil, VIX, equities and price-path context; Confidence stays in the medium-low band to reflect that reduced evidence base and the continued absence of a directly-confirmed live NQ/QQQ intraday chart, partially offset by solid multi-source corroboration on futures levels, Asia breadth, VIX and yields this run. Tail eases slightly to 9% (calm continuation, no persistent one-way structure, firmer but still orderly Asia carry-through) and Stress eases to 23% as the quiet handover persists, though the approaching Retail Sales, cash open and preliminary UMich sentiment cluster keeps the forecast Stress path rising into early afternoon UTC before easing back through the evening and into the next Asia handover.",
